BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Brattleboro House Concert: Doozy Jane
DTSTART:20260913T160000
DTEND:20260913T180000
DTSTAMP:20260913T145649Z
UID:2413b16e07d7d5bead8ae9378ab39e@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Doozy Jane is a quartet rooted in traditions of American harmo
 ny singing and swingy\, fiddle-driven string bands. With intricate four-pa
 rt treble vocals\, they specialize in songs written by women and queer art
 ists. Along with their original songs\, they draw from a repertoire of oft
 en lesser-known but beautifully crafted covers that show their taste for t
 he flavors of swing and gospel and an ear for the unconventional. Named in
  part for their arranger Anna Patton’s grandmother Jane who loved to sin
 g the tricky inner harmonies of barbershop quartets\, the quartet clearly 
 shares a mutual love for “a doozy of a song.” Bass guitar\, tenor guit
 ar\, twin fiddles\, and clarinet round out their arrangements. The musicia
 ns: Anna Patton (vocals\, clarinet\, and tenor guitar) is a performer\, si
 nging leader\, composer\, and arranger. She directs two choruses in Brattl
 eboro Vermont. The Soubrettes\, under the umbrella of the Vermont Jazz Cen
 ter and Brattleboro Harmonia (formerly the Brattleboro Women’s Chorus). 
 Her soulful\, swingy clarinet playing has been a feature of Zara Bode’s 
 Little Big Band\, the internationally touring dance band Elixir\, and many
  other bands and recording projects. Haley Anderson (vocals and bass guita
 r) grew up covering classic rock songs in the basement with her siblings. 
 She got her musical start playing saxophone and singing in community choir
 s\, eventually touring Europe and the US with Vermont’s Northern Harmony
  ensemble. Haley's path to bass guitar was less deliberate — during a Do
 ozy Jane rehearsal\, her bandmates held a vote while she was in the bathro
 om\, and she emerged to find herself the band's new bassist. Away from the
  stage\, she dabbles at earning a living in bookkeeping and graphic design
 . Julia Read (vocals\, violin\, guitar) is a musician and performer living
  in Western Massachusetts. Her desire to sing in harmony led her to join T
 he Soubrettes chorus\, where she met the friends that would eventually bec
 ome Doozy Jane. Julia has recorded three albums (https://juliaread.bandcam
 p.com/) and is in the process of making another. Locally\, she has perform
 ed with The Royal Frog Ballet and Theatre Truck. She works as a speech and
  language pathologist with adults. Sarah-Hadley Yakir (vocals\, fiddle) is
  a hybrid player of classical violin and contemporary fiddle. She tours wi
 dely with her folk-trad band River Road\, whose debut album Over The Moon 
 will be released later this year. After joining Anna Patton’s Soubrettes
 \, Sarah couldn’t get enough of the unique challenges and satisfying cru
 nch of close harmony singing—enter Doozy Jane. Off stage\, she likes to 
 walk up big hills and hang out with her tuxedo cat. GET A TASTE HERE! http
 s://www.youtube.com/shorts/7JUY9f14QWc Facebook Event Page: https://www.fa
 cebook.com/events/1589185579573603/ Under the Maple Suggestion donation $2
 0-$30\; any amount welcome\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Vermont Public is independent\, community-supported media\, servi
 ng Vermont with trusted\, relevant and essential information. We share sto
 ries that bring people together\, from every corner of our region.\, © 20
 26 Vermont Public | 365 Troy Ave. Colchester\, VT 05446
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/brattlebor
 o-house-concert-doozy-jane-11-08-2026-20-06-17
END:VEVENT
