BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:WORDS OUT LOUD: Don’t Forget To Write\, reading series with Mich
 ael Dumanis & Sasha Hom
DTSTART:20260913T150000
DTEND:20260913T160000
DTSTAMP:20260913T145649Z
UID:1b7c13c1883aa4564bf4b7bdb75c02@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Art at the Kent Presents WORDS OUT LOUD As part of event offer
 ings for Art at the Kent’s 2026 exhibit Throughlines at the Kents’ Cor
 ner State Historic Site\, WORDS OUT LOUD\, the popular Sunday afternoon fa
 ll reading series\, returns to the Old West Church. For this year’s firs
 t of three readings\, WORDS OUT LOUD: Don’t Forget to Write\, welcomes V
 ermont poets Michael Dumanis (poetry) and Sasha Hom (fiction). To say “D
 on’t Forget to Write” is to remind travelers to “stay in touch\,” 
 to "send word" from afar\, wherever they are. This year’s authors rememb
 er to write\, and they do so creatively and intelligently in poetry and pr
 ose. Readings will be followed by receptions down the road at the Kent ami
 dst the art on display for this year’s exhibit “Throughlines” where 
 attendees may meet and chat with the authors and a selection of books will
  be available in the shop. The WORDS OUT LOUD readings take place at the O
 ld West Church at 3 o’clock. Guests should arrive early to allow time fo
 r parking and seating at this historic 200-year-old meetinghouse in rural 
 Calais\, bring layers for warmth\, and leave pets at home. Open to all. Do
 nations welcome at the door. With a few steps up into the vestibule\, the 
 historic Old West Church is not ADA accessible at this time. About the Wri
 ters September 13: Sasha Hom is a writer\, goat farmer\, yurt dweller\, an
 d homeschooling mother of four. She earned her MFA from Warren Wilson Coll
 ege as a Holden Minority Scholar. Her first novella\, Sidework\, published
  by Black Lawrence Press\, was a New Immigrant Writing Series selection an
 d winner of the 2025 Vermont Book Award in Fiction. She’s received suppo
 rt from the Elizabeth George Foundation\, Sustainable Arts Foundation\, Ve
 rmont Arts Council\, and Friends of Writers and won the Brink Literary Jou
 rnal Award for Hybrid Writing. Her work can be found at The Millions\, Kwe
 li Journal\, Literary Mama\, Leon Literary Review\, and elsewhere. Michael
  Dumanis is the author of Creature (Four Way Books\, 2023)\, a finalist fo
 r the 2023 Vermont Book Award in Poetry\, the National Jewish Book Award\,
  and the Big Other Book Award. He is the author of one previous collection
 \, My Soviet Union\, winner of the Juniper Prize for Poetry\, and the coed
 itor of the anthology Legitimate Dangers: American Poets of the New Centur
 y. He was born in the former Soviet Union and lived there until his parent
 s were granted political asylum in the United States. He now lives in Nort
 h Bennington\, Vermont\, where he teaches at Bennington College and serves
  as editor of Bennington Review. WORDS OUT LOUD 2026 has been organized by
  poet Mary Elder Jacobsen with the support of the Art at the Kent curatori
 al team.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Old West Church\, 758 Old West Church Road
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/words-out-
 loud-dont-forget-to-write-reading-series-with-michael-dumanis-amp-sasha-ho
 m-19-08-2026-10-31-43
END:VEVENT
